{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtRkoncgMR2m4cF5fif9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish returned 500 because `similar[].score` was a Python float, which boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects. The fix is in place and the tests pass.\n\n**Cause:** `similarity()` returns a float, and `related()` stored it as `score`. The first publish had an empty table, so `similar` was `[]` and nothing float-typed was written. The second publish found one existing story, produced a float, and `put_item` raised `TypeError: Float types are not supported`. The handler turned that into a 500. The existing test only publishes one story, so it never reached this path.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `src/app.py`: `related()` stores the score as `Decimal(str(...))`. A new `to_dynamo()` helper converts any float in the item to `Decimal` recursively, and `publish()` applies it before `put_item`, so a future float field can't bring this back.\n- `tests/test_publish.py`: added a test that publishes two stories through `handler()` and expects 201 with a `Decimal` score, plus a test for the conversion helper. Both new tests fail on the original code and pass with the fix. `python3 -m unittest discover tests` reports 3 passing.\n- `ANSWER.md`: cause and fix, as requested.\n\nI didn't commit, deploy, or publish anything, and `logs/error.log` is unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":939,"cache_read_input_tokens":30850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":939},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a599f385-456c-4296-88b7-1b67cd349cba","uuid":"cbbd48d5-a80b-4e2c-8bfd-1f3d52ace9b8","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:04:52.115Z","